{"role":"user","content":"I need you to research the following facts using webfetch and websearch tools:\n\n1. The Greenland shark (Somniosus microcephalus) is known as the longest-lived vertebrate. It is named after the island of Greenland.\n\n2. According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what was the 2020 estimated population of Greenland (the island), to the nearest thousand?\n\nPlease:\n- Use webfetch to access the Wikipedia page for Greenland (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland)\n- Look for population estimates, specifically the 2020 estimate\n- The answer should be to the nearest thousand (e.g., 56,000 or 57,000)\n- Also confirm that the Greenland shark is indeed the longest-lived vertebrate\n\nReport back with the exact population figure you find."}
